  "caption_strategy": "Lead with a curiosity/hype hook that makes a non-follower stop. Name the game plainly for search. Keep it 1-2 short lines. Always credit the streamer/clipper. End with the follow CTA. No generic mega-tags.",
  "hashtag_strategy": "4-5 niche tags matching the game (e.g. #gtarp #gta6 #nopixel for GTA; #valorant #valorantclips for VALORANT). Vary two per post. Avoid #gaming/#viral mega-tags.",
  "learnings": "Data remains very thin (zero follows/visits across all 18+ posts; no cell yet converts past reach). **Retention is still the only signal.** Among cells ≥8 posts: **Valorant** leads everything — twitch|Valorant retention 0.619, reach 110, shares firing; prioritise every available slot. **Hour 21** (retention 0.589) and **hour 10** (retention 0.456, highest shares 0.0044) are your best posting windows — favour them. **Western** (retention 0.45) beats **Asian** (0.419) but Asian|Valorant (retention 0.583) is a genuine bright spot — keep those Asian Valorant slots. **Halo** (retention 0.481, saves 0.003 — best save rate in the dataset) earns its slots; keep it. **Drop Splatoon Raiders** — retention 0.272, reach ~29, dead weight. **Arc Raiders and Hell Let Loose** are new with no data yet; post and hold judgment. **Smart-trim**: trim:off (retention 0.444, reach 77.8) beats trim:on (0.436, reach 47) — keep trim OFF as default, pause the test. **Early-velocity**: ev_arm:on (retention 0.475, views/reach 1.322) vs ev_arm:off (retention 0.425, views/reach 1.248) — positive directional signal on both metrics in the unbiased cells; keep running, do not conclude yet (6 vs 12 posts). **Caption writers**: open with visceral hook (\"bro said no 💀 / there is literally no way\"), credit creator in line 2, close with \"Follow @clipkroniek 🎮 #Valorant #HaloEvolved #ArcRaiders #gaming\" — put the game name in line 1 for search.",
